                    <p class="mt-3">
                        Denmark is home to a range of public and private universities that welcome international students with open arms. These <b>Denmark universities for international students</b> provide a rich blend of cultural diversity and academic excellence.
                    </p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>
                            <b>Popular Universities for International Students:</b> Universities like the University of Southern Denmark and Roskilde University focus on integrating diverse student communities. They offer a broad spectrum of programs specifically designed to suit international students.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <b>Study in Denmark for Indian Students:</b> Denmark is turning into a hotspot for Indian students due to programs catering to specialised fields, competitive tuition fees, and numerous scholarship opportunities. Denmark also allows international students, including those from India, to work part-time during their studies, making it financially accessible.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <b>State-of-the-Art Research Facilities:</b> Most Danish universities are well-equipped with world-class laboratories and research facilities, providing students ample opportunities to innovate and experiment.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <b>Sustainability in Education:</b> Denmark is a global leader in sustainability, a concept that is deeply integrated into its higher education programs, especially for disciplines like environmental science and green technology.
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>
                        Studying at Denmark universities doesn’t just give you access to a premier education system, but also the chance to live in one of the most progressive and inclusive societies in the world.
                    </p>
